/-!
# The Lubin–Tate level is generated by one primitive division point

Milne's Theorem I.3.1 (Serre, *Local Fields*, Ch. XV §4) says that the `π^n`-torsion `Λ_n` of the
Lubin–Tate group is a free `𝒪[F]/π^n`-module of rank one.  Its structural consequence, and the one
the reciprocity theory uses, is that **the level `K_n = F(Λ_n)` is generated by any single primitive
division point**:

`K_n = F(π_n)`  for  `π_n ∈ Λ_n ∖ Λ_{n-1}`,

whence `[K_n : F] = (q-1)q^{n-1}` (the degree of the Eisenstein polynomial `f^{[n-1]}`) and
`#Gal(K_n/F) = (q-1)q^{n-1}`.

This file isolates that consequence as the *named hypothesis*

`NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTLevelIsSimple F π q n`,

and *proves* the degree and Galois-order statements from it.  The hypothesis is a single concrete
statement about the sets `Λ_n ⊆ F̄` built in `LubinTate/DivisionPoints.lean`; it is strictly weaker
than the classical modular statement of Milne I.3.1, it is a theorem in the cases `q = 2`, `n = 1`
(see `Audit/LevelSimplicity_padic.lean`), and it follows from the `𝒪[F]`-module structure
`Λ_n ≅ (𝒪[F]/π^n)^+` together with its compatibility with the Galois action (Milne, *CFT*, Theorem
I.3.1, §I.3).

## Main results

* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTLevel_eq_adjoin_singleton_of_isSimple`;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.finrank_LTLevel_eq_of_isSimple`;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.card_aut_LTLevel_eq_of_isSimple`.
-/

open Polynomial

namespace NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate

universe u

/-- **The simplicity of the Lubin–Tate level** (the structural consequence of Milne I.3.1): every
division point of level `n` is contained in the field generated by a *primitive* division point.

In the classical theory this holds because `Λ_n` is a free `𝒪[F]/π^n`-module of rank one generated
by any `π_n ∈ Λ_n ∖ Λ_{n-1}`, and the Galois action on `Λ_n` is the action of the units
`(𝒪[F]/π^n)^×`. -/
def LTLevelIsSimple (F : Type u) [Field F] (π : F) (q n : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ y : AlgebraicClosure F, y ∈ LTdivisionSet F π q n → y ∉ LTdivisionSet F π q (n - 1) →
    LTdivisionSet F π q n ⊆
      (IntermediateField.adjoin F ({y} : Set (AlgebraicClosure F)) : Set (AlgebraicClosure F))

/-- **Under simplicity, the level is generated by one primitive division point.** -/
theorem LTLevel_eq_adjoin_singleton_of_isSimple {F : Type u} [Field F] {π : F} {q n : ℕ}
    (h : LTLevelIsSimple F π q n) {y : AlgebraicClosure F} (hy : y ∈ LTdivisionSet F π q n)
    (hpr : y ∉ LTdivisionSet F π q (n - 1)) :
    LTLevel F π q n = IntermediateField.adjoin F ({y} : Set (AlgebraicClosure F)) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [LTLevel, IntermediateField.adjoin_le_iff]
    exact h y hy hpr
  · rw [IntermediateField.adjoin_le_iff]
    intro z hz
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hz
    subst hz
    exact LTdivisionSet_subset_LTLevel F π q n hy

end NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate
